Yakumo v@VERSION@ for Windows x86-64

1. Extract the entire folder.
2. Run Yakumo.exe.
3. On first start, choose the disc image from your own legally obtained copy of
   Monster Hunter Portable 3rd HD Ver.

This is the portable version: because of portable.txt, Yakumo keeps its
settings, saves and game data in the data folder next to Yakumo.exe, and
nothing in %APPDATA%. Keep the folder somewhere you can write to (not in
Program Files); a USB drive works. Saves are under data\ms0\PSP\SAVEDATA.
If Yakumo is already set up on this computer, the first start offers to copy
that data here; the original stays where it is.
Delete portable.txt and move the data folder away to use %APPDATA% instead.
Press Esc, or L3+R3 on a gamepad, to open the Yakumo menu.

A Vulkan-capable graphics driver is required. SDL3, FFmpeg and the Microsoft
Visual C++ runtime DLLs are included.
This archive contains no game assets, disc image, executable from the game or saves.
